  "strategy": "Approach and rationale:\nThe goal is to minimize the maximum overlap between a step function and its shifts on the interval [0,2]. The previous solution achieved 0.380865, while a theoretical lower bound suggests 0.3808. The current method uses binary representations, which may not fully exploit smooth optimizations. Here, we use a multi-cycle sinusoidal representation with harmonics to dynamically adapt frequency content. This allows for smoother transitions and more effective frequency cancellations between shifts. The key idea is to:\n1. Represent the function using harmonic components to mimic wavelet-like cancellations\n2. Use constrained optimization to maintain integral sum exactly\n3. Temporally adapt the most promising frequency components\n4. Fast prototype by leveraging symmetry and linearity\n\nMathematical specification:\nFor samples x_i, define the function:\nh(x) = 0.5 + \u03a3_{k=1}^{K} A_k * sin(2\u03c0kx + \u03c6_k) \nsubject to:\n- Integral constraint: \u03a3_{i} h_i = n/2\n- Bounds: 0 \u2264 h_i \u2264 1\n\nOverlap objective: max_k \u222b h(x)\u00b7(1-h(x+k)) dx = max_k (mean shift overlap)\n\nImplementation procedure:\n1. Initialization:\n   - If parent available, project to harmonic space\n   - Else use uniform distribution temperatures\n2. Forward model: compute samples from harmonics\n3. Optimization:\n\n   while time_remaining:\n        - Select active frequencies based on amplitude variance\n        - Use randomized simplex optimization per active harmonic\n        - Temporal adaptation by updating weights by gradient descent\n        - Local refinement via L-BFGS along constraints\n        - Feasibility repair by clipping and rescaling\n\n        - Maintain best candidate at each generation\n        - Terminate when no improvement for multiple generations\n\nSearch choices:\n- Harmonics: 10-25 (varying per run)\n- Amplitude range: [-0.4,0.4]\n- Temperature schedule cooling exponential\n\nComputebudget:\n- Primary search: 80 us/candidate\n- 1000 seconds = 133 candidates\n- Fallback: binary representation if stuck\n\nValidation:\n- Compute exact integral\n- Ensure samples in [0,1]\n- Project to feasible space if needed\n\nReturn contract:\n- Adhere to interface\n- Return (h_values, c5_bound, n_points)\n- Optimize with sparse representation",
